findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA mentions 'silent error swallowing' in security tests but the specific
    issue of from_file_or_default swallowing parse/permission errors was not flagged.
    The reviewer did not mention this pattern. Dev likely implemented unwrap_or_default()
    without distinguishing NotFound from other errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA lists 'CWE-209 error exposure' in the security.rs test file covering
    error exposure. However, the reviewer did not explicitly flag the eprintln Display
    leak, and main.rs is a no-op so errors never reach stderr anyway. Partial catch
    via test design intent.
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote siem_client.rs tests covering 'CWE-113 header injection' and\
    \ the reviewer verified 'CWE-113 header injection protection exists for token\
    \ and tenant at client.rs:26-38'. However, the specific issue of using raw String\
    \ instead of TenantId from axiathon-core was not flagged \u2014 the fix was newline\
    \ rejection, not type-safe TenantId usage. Partial catch."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer verified 'Workspace dependencies correctly declared in root Cargo.toml:52-58'
    but did not check whether individual crate Cargo.toml uses workspace = true vs
    direct version strings. The 6 deps using direct versions were not flagged.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged: '[HIGH] RawConfig uses #[derive(Deserialize)] with\
    \ deny_unknown_fields absent \u2014 unknown fields silently ignored at config.rs:7-12'\
    \ and specifically noted 'a user who thinks their token is being loaded from config\
    \ gets zero feedback. Consider #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]'."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). TEA wrote config_loading.rs tests but the specific assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...) anti-pattern was not flagged by any phase.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. TEA designed 149 tests but this specific test quality issue
    was not caught.
